{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MXvJDyYcgdvRkvi4xsz2nX","type":"tool_result","content":"{\n  \"searched_issues\": 1537,\n  \"quarantined\": 0,\n  \"threshold\": 0.35,\n  \"candidates\": [\n    {\n      \"number\": 2015,\n      \"score\": 0.198,\n      \"title\": \"Thank you note!\",\n      \"state\": \"closed\",\n      \"state_reason\": \"completed\",\n      \"strong\": false,\n      \"excerpt\": \"This is waaaaay too cool thank you! ![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/9364931/156361507-ef070a94-d21a-43a9-81bb-c8ad27ee7d48.png) (I'm working on a Pelican plugin and Pelican uses Rich to format the stacktraces)\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 1022,\n      \"score\": 0.154,\n      \"title\": \"Progress on generator\",\n      \"state\": \"closed\",\n      \"state_reason\": \"completed\",\n      \"strong\": false,\n      \"excerpt\": \"Hi @willmcgugan , I hope to find you well. Thank you for this amazing library. I was wondering how can I use the `progress.track` function to track a generator since `total` is required but generators have no length. Thank you. Cheers, Francesco\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 1076,\n      \"score\": 0.147,\n      \"title\": \"Double Live Tables?\",\n      \"state\": \"closed\",\n      \"state_reason\": \"completed\",\n      \"strong\": false,\n      \"excerpt\": \"Trying to print out two live tables with different headers/column count. Apparently can't stack double live tables. ``` with Live(generate_table(), refresh_per_second=4) as live: with Live(generate_table2(), refresh_per_second=4) as live2: while True: sleep(0.4) live.update(generate_table()) live2.update(generate_table2()) ``` ``` \\\"Only one live display may be active at once\\\" ``` What is the workaround? Thank you!\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2158,\n      \"score\": 0.144,\n      \"title\": \"Rich Live display not updating the terminal \",\n      \"state\": \"closed\",\n      \"state_reason\": \"completed\",\n      \"strong\": false,\n      \"excerpt\": \"Hi, I hope everyone is ok, I am trying to display multiple progress bars with Rich. My program uses python concurrent.futures.ProcessPoolExecutor to run multiple tasks at the same time. I am using a table to display the progress bars, the table and progress bars are displayed correctly in the terminal, but all progress bars remain at zero until the end. ```python import concurrent.futures task_progress = Progress( \\\"{task.description}\\\", SpinnerColumn(), BarColumn(), TextColumn(\\\"[progress.percentage]{task.percentage:>3.0f}%\\\"), ) def process_chunk( chunk: list[tuple, None, None], comparison_index ...\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 3207,\n      \"score\": 0.127,\n      \"title\": \"[BUG]When there are too many progress bars, all progress bars cannot be displayed\",\n      \"state\": \"open\",\n      \"state_reason\": null,\n      \"strong\": false,\n      \"excerpt\": \"- [x] I've checked [docs](https://rich.readthedocs.io/en/latest/introduction.html) and [closed issues](https://github.com/Textualize/rich/issues?q=is%3Aissue+is%3Aclosed) for possible solutions. - [x] I can't find my issue in the [FAQ](https://github.com/Textualize/rich/blob/master/FAQ.md). **Describe the bug** My program needs to display multiple progress bars. When the progress bar fills the entire screen, the remaining progress bars will not be displayed until all progress bars are completed. ![1700288051394](https://github.com/Textualize/rich/assets/49263334/9ee6965e-d94f-44db-bbdf-6f5932c ...\"\n    }\n  ]\n}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7b423bba-cc6e-49d2-a509-c2d7f4760768","uuid":"4822f3fa-26b4-480d-a3a1-c689bfc413d4","timestamp":"2026-10-26T10:23:40.812Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"{\n  \"searched_issues\": 1537,\n  \"quarantined\": 0,\n  \"threshold\": 0.35,\n  \"candidates\": [\n    {\n      \"number\": 2015,\n      \"score\": 0.198,\n      \"title\": \"Thank you note!\",\n      \"state\": 